///1BIDUMP

BIDUMP Version 1.23
by Charlie Godet-Ceraolo (10/04/84)
  IBM customization by Kirk Lawrence

BIDUMP lets you browse through any file at the byte level -- going either
forward or backward -- one record at a time, in "split-screen" format.
BIDUMP displays the file's hex code on the left side of the screen, and
the ASCII equivalent on the right side of the screen ("Norton"-type format).
Any record can also be sent to the printer, if desired.


///2USAGE
Syntax: BIDUMP filename.ext  <ENTER>


///2KEYS
Once BIDUMP has loaded the file you've specified, the following keys
control the action within the program:

   F or <SPACE> to go forward.
   B to go backward.
   1 for beginning (first record) of file.
   E for end (last record) of file.
   C for continuous forward scroll.
   P to PRINT current sector.
   Q or X to exit.
